            "typeClass": "compound",
            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "<p>The research was conducted to design a similar experiment to the experiment by Garrett, Lazzaro, Ariely & Sharot (2016). In this experiment the escalation of dishonesty is measured by letting a participant advise another person on how many pennies are in a jar. In some cases overestimating or underestimating the amount in a jar can lead to monetary benefits for the participant.</p><p>For this experiment, see the article \"The brain adapts to dishonesty\": <a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/nn.4426.\" target=\"_blank\">https://https://www.nature.com/articles/nn.4426.</a> DOI: 10.3389/fnins.2020.00502</p><p><br></p><p>The pictures have been published for re-use and have not been yet used for a scientific paper. This due to the team pursuing different research topics.</p><p><br></p>"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
